WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.421
Welcome. This video shows how to work with the DRMD AI Generator.

00:00:05.641 --> 00:00:14.134
A DRMD, or Digital Reference Material Document, is the machine-readable
form of a reference material certificate or product information sheet.

00:00:14.354 --> 00:00:20.197
The generator creates these files. We will go through
every feature, step by step, with a real certificate.

00:00:22.397 --> 00:00:28.729
The generator is a web page. Open it in Google
Chrome or Microsoft Edge. There is nothing to install.

00:00:28.949 --> 00:00:35.763
You can also download the generator as a single HTML file
and open it from your computer. It works the same way.

00:00:35.983 --> 00:00:40.861
Everything runs in your browser. There is no server,
and your documents are not stored anywhere.

00:00:41.761 --> 00:00:45.862
The generator opens on the Home page. It shows the three ways to work.

00:00:46.082 --> 00:00:51.367
One: enter a DRMD by hand. You need no AI and no API key for this.

00:00:51.587 --> 00:00:58.701
Two: convert PDF documents with AI. You can
convert a single PDF, or all PDFs of a folder at once.

00:00:58.921 --> 00:01:03.646
Three: open an existing DRMD XML file, edit it, and save it again.

00:01:04.546 --> 00:01:09.496
The screen has two parts. The left side shows the PDF. The right side shows the form.

00:01:09.716 --> 00:01:16.595
The buttons at the top start each way of working:
New DRMD, Upload PDF, Upload folder, and Import XML.

00:01:16.815 --> 00:01:20.031
The bar at the bottom always shows the state of your document.

00:01:20.931 --> 00:01:24.632
To convert PDFs with AI, open AI settings first.

00:01:24.852 --> 00:01:31.085
The generator reads each certificate with an AI
model that understands both text and page images.

00:01:30.885 --> 00:01:36.371
You can choose from six AI providers, for example Google Gemini, OpenAI or Anthropic.

00:01:36.591 --> 00:01:41.046
You use your own API key. The usage is billed to your account with that provider.

00:01:41.946 --> 00:01:50.934
Paste your key into the field of the provider. Keys are kept only while this browser
tab is open. They are never saved, and each key is sent only to its own provider.

00:01:51.154 --> 00:01:58.166
Click Check key. The generator asks the provider if the key works,
and shows how many models of this key can read the certificates.

00:01:58.386 --> 00:02:05.892
Keep the model on Automatic. The generator then uses a fast,
low-cost model, and switches to the next one if a model is busy.

00:02:06.112 --> 00:02:14.079
Below, you find notes on data protection, speed and prices for this
provider. Please read them before you send confidential documents.

00:02:14.979 --> 00:02:21.976
Now let us convert a certificate. Click Upload PDF, and
choose the file. You can also drag a PDF onto the left side.

00:02:22.196 --> 00:02:29.274
In this example, we use the certificate of the reference
material BAM-M386a, pure copper, from BAM.

00:02:29.494 --> 00:02:35.783
If you upload a PDF before you enter a key, the generator
waits. It starts by itself as soon as the key works.

00:02:36.083 --> 00:02:42.569
The AI now reads the whole document. This usually takes
less than a minute. In this video, the waiting time is shortened.

00:02:42.789 --> 00:02:46.346
Then the certificate opens on the left, and the form is filled in.

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:53.268
In the background, the generator looks up identifiers for the producer
and for every substance. You can already start your review.

00:02:54.168 --> 00:03:02.093
AI settings now shows the Usage table: the AI requests of this tab,
with the tokens, the cost, and the average time per request.

00:03:02.993 --> 00:03:11.509
Use the arrows to move between the pages. With minus and plus, you zoom
in and out. You can rotate a page, or enlarge the PDF to the whole window.

00:03:11.729 --> 00:03:17.471
Drag the divider to give more space to the PDF or to
the form. Double-click it to go back to the middle.

00:03:17.691 --> 00:03:26.716
The data is organised in tabs, in the same order as a DRMD: administrative
data, materials, properties, statements, and comments and documents.

00:03:26.516 --> 00:03:29.431
The last tab validates and exports the file.

00:03:30.331 --> 00:03:38.294
Let us start with the administrative data. The title tells whether the
document is a reference material certificate or a product information sheet.

00:03:38.514 --> 00:03:46.259
Every document gets a unique identifier. If the certificate has none,
the generator creates a UUID. This button creates a new one.

00:03:46.479 --> 00:03:51.619
Fields with a red star are required by the DRMD schema or by the official rules.

00:03:52.519 --> 00:03:59.756
Every field name is also a link. Click a name, and the DRMD
guidance document opens at the matching section, in a new tab.

00:04:00.156 --> 00:04:03.216
Here you can read what the element means and how to fill it in.

00:04:03.516 --> 00:04:06.736
Then switch back to the generator. Your work stays open.

00:04:07.636 --> 00:04:13.815
The period of validity comes from the certificate.
This certificate is valid until the end of 2050.

00:04:14.035 --> 00:04:20.401
Next to most fields, you see a locate button. Click it, and
the place in the PDF where the value comes from is marked.

00:04:20.621 --> 00:04:29.834
Here, the certificate says 12/2050. The panel explains that the date was written in
the ISO format, year, month and day (2050-12-31), so that software can read it.

00:04:30.054 --> 00:04:34.584
Such a conversion for machine readability is normal, and it is not marked for checking.

00:04:35.484 --> 00:04:42.514
Some certificates are valid for a period after dispatch instead. Then
you choose Time After Dispatch, and enter the years and months.

00:04:42.734 --> 00:04:53.186
The period is written in the ISO 8601 format, for example P1Y for one year.
The dispatch date is not on the certificate, so it stays empty unless you fill it in.

00:04:55.686 --> 00:05:00.706
The reference material producer is filled in with
the name, the contact details and the address.

00:05:00.926 --> 00:05:06.176
Use the locate button to check any field. Here, the email address is marked on page 6.

00:05:06.396 --> 00:05:10.085
The country is written as a two-letter code, here DE for Germany.

00:05:10.985 --> 00:05:18.848
Now data enrichment. The generator found the producer in the
Research Organization Registry, ROR, and added its ROR ID.

00:05:19.148 --> 00:05:26.334
Click the link icon to open the record, and check that it is the producer
of the certificate. With the search button, you can look it up again.

00:05:27.234 --> 00:05:31.573
The responsible persons are the people who approved the certificate, with their roles.

00:05:31.793 --> 00:05:37.371
The main signer is ticked. Here, it is Dr. S. Richter, from the Committee for Certification.

00:05:38.271 --> 00:05:46.674
The Materials tab describes the reference material: its name, the RM code,
the material identifier, the class, the description and the quantities.

00:05:46.894 --> 00:05:55.612
The minimum sample size on the certificate is 0.2 grams. Below the
field, you see how it is written in the XML, with the D-SI unit for gram.

00:05:55.832 --> 00:06:02.537
For a defined chemical substance, the generator adds the
CAS number and the InChIKey here. A copper alloy has none.

00:06:03.437 --> 00:06:09.197
The material identifier holds the lot or batch number.
This certificate gives none, so the field is empty.

00:06:09.417 --> 00:06:14.660
This identifier matters, because it links a material
to its values. We will come back to it later.

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:19.115
The Properties tab holds the measured values, in property sets.

00:06:19.335 --> 00:06:25.149
This set holds the certified values, so Certified
is ticked, and the set has a green line on the left.

00:06:25.369 --> 00:06:31.723
The Linked material says which material these values
belong to. This certificate has one material, pure copper.

00:06:31.943 --> 00:06:36.598
Each property set has one or more tables. Every table has a name and a description.

00:06:36.398 --> 00:06:42.126
The description keeps the footnotes of the certificate,
for example how the uncertainty was calculated.

00:06:43.026 --> 00:06:50.957
In the table, each row is one quantity: the name, the identifiers,
the value, the uncertainty, the unit as printed, and the D-SI unit.

00:06:51.177 --> 00:06:55.563
The table is wider than the form. Scroll to the right to see the last two columns.

00:06:55.783 --> 00:06:59.395
They are the coverage factor, k, and the coverage probability, P.

00:06:59.615 --> 00:07:08.072
The footnote of the certificate says: k equals 2, with a
level of confidence of about 95 %. So k is 2, and P is 0.95.

00:07:08.972 --> 00:07:19.082
Click a value of P. The footnote is marked in the PDF, and the panel
explains that 95 % is written as 0.95, a number between 0 and 1.

00:07:19.302 --> 00:07:29.312
The uncertainty, k and P are checked while you type. If k is missing, the field is outlined
in red, with a short note: enter k too, or clear P. An expanded uncertainty needs both.

00:07:29.532 --> 00:07:32.030
When you enter k again, the note disappears.

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:36.459
Now the units. The certificate prints milligrams per kilogram (mg/kg).

00:07:36.679 --> 00:07:45.373
The generator writes every unit also as a D-SI unit, the unit format
of the DRMD XML, so that software can read it without doubt.

00:07:45.593 --> 00:07:56.310
Click a D-SI unit. The unit is marked in the PDF, and the panel explains how it was
written: its quality class, here gold, and the rules of the D-SI guide, with page numbers.

00:07:56.530 --> 00:08:05.124
The class tells how close the unit is to the SI. Platinum uses SI base
units only. Gold also uses prefixes and derived units, such as milligram.

00:08:04.924 --> 00:08:11.186
Silver uses units accepted with the SI, such as the
litre, and bronze uses older units, such as the bar.

00:08:12.086 --> 00:08:20.047
If you change a unit, the D-SI unit is updated at once. Here, grams
per kilogram (g/kg) gives a new D-SI unit. Let us change it back.

00:08:20.267 --> 00:08:27.360
Units outside the SI, such as pounds or degrees Fahrenheit,
are converted to the SI, and the value as printed is kept next to it.

00:08:27.160 --> 00:08:32.597
Notes like dry mass are kept out of the unit, and
the report reminds you to keep them in the name.

00:08:32.817 --> 00:08:38.435
If the rules cannot decide on a unit, the AI is asked,
and its answer is checked by the same rules.

00:08:39.335 --> 00:08:43.982
For every element, the generator looked up the CAS Registry Number and the InChIKey.

00:08:44.202 --> 00:08:52.715
Each identifier is a link. The CAS number opens CAS Common Chemistry,
and the InChIKey opens PubChem, so you can check the substance.

00:08:52.935 --> 00:08:58.750
With the pencil, you can edit the identifiers of a row. The
search button in the column header looks them up again.

00:08:59.650 --> 00:09:06.396
Further down is a second property set, values for information.
These values are not certified, so Certified is not ticked.

00:09:06.616 --> 00:09:10.274
You can add rows, tables and property sets by hand at any time.

00:09:11.174 --> 00:09:17.093
The Statements tab holds the standard statements
that ISO 17034 expects on a certificate:

00:09:16.893 --> 00:09:22.362
the intended use, commutability, storage, handling, and metrological traceability.

00:09:22.582 --> 00:09:26.991
As before, the locate button shows where each statement comes from in the PDF.

00:09:27.211 --> 00:09:31.152
Anything else that the certificate states can be added under Other statements.

00:09:32.052 --> 00:09:35.534
On the Comment & documents tab, you can write a general comment.

00:09:35.754 --> 00:09:44.142
The certificate itself is attached automatically. It is marked as the
human-readable PDF certificate, and it is embedded in the XML file.

00:09:44.362 --> 00:09:48.471
You can attach more PDF files, for example a certification report.

00:09:49.371 --> 00:09:55.942
Now a very important feature. The generator compares
every value that the AI filled in with the text of the PDF.

00:09:56.162 --> 00:10:03.068
A value that does not appear word for word is outlined in amber.
The tab and the status bar show how many values are left to check.

00:10:03.288 --> 00:10:12.748
Here, the AI reworded the description of the material. Click the locate button. The
passage is marked in the PDF, and the panel names the word that is not in it: copper.

00:10:12.548 --> 00:10:14.885
It appears in another place of the PDF.

00:10:15.105 --> 00:10:21.241
The meaning is correct. So click Mark as verified. The
amber outline disappears, and the counters go down.

00:10:21.461 --> 00:10:26.963
If you edit a value yourself, it also counts as verified.
Values that you type in are never marked.

00:10:27.863 --> 00:10:30.362
Finally, open Validate & export.

00:10:30.582 --> 00:10:36.808
The first box, AI conversion, counts the values still
to check. This is about the content that the AI read.

00:10:37.028 --> 00:10:47.157
The second box checks the XML against the DRMD schema, version 1.0.0,
and the official business rules. This document is valid and ready to export.

00:10:48.057 --> 00:10:57.732
Every finding has a level. An error must be corrected before the file is valid.
A conditional rule applies only in some cases, for example a commutability statement.

00:10:57.532 --> 00:10:58.708
A note is a hint.

00:10:58.928 --> 00:11:04.519
For a conditional rule, ask yourself: does this apply
to my material? If it does, add the information.

00:11:05.419 --> 00:11:12.449
Let us see an error. If the name of the producer is deleted, the tab
and the status bar turn red, and the report says what is missing.

00:11:12.669 --> 00:11:17.472
When the name is entered again, the document
is valid again. Every change is checked at once.

00:11:18.372 --> 00:11:24.361
Under DRMD XML, click View to see the XML itself. Save XML downloads the file.

00:11:24.581 --> 00:11:30.481
The HTML report shows the same data in a
readable form. You can view it and save it as well.

00:11:30.701 --> 00:11:36.864
To publish the certificate in the COMAR database,
save both files, sign in to COMAR, and upload them there.

00:11:37.084 --> 00:11:44.355
The generator does not sign the file. Sign or seal the finished
XML afterwards, with the signing software of your organisation.

00:11:44.575 --> 00:11:50.172
And please remember: data extracted with AI must
always be reviewed before you use or publish it.

00:11:51.072 --> 00:11:56.142
To convert many documents at once, click
Upload folder. A note explains what happens.

00:11:56.362 --> 00:12:04.765
Choose the folder with the PDF files. Your browser then asks for permission
to edit files in this folder. Choose Allow, so that the results can be saved.

00:12:05.465 --> 00:12:17.308
The PDFs are converted one after another. For every PDF, the DRMD XML and the
HTML report are saved into the same folder, right next to it. Your PDFs stay as they are.

00:12:17.528 --> 00:12:22.854
If a run stops, upload the same folder again.
PDFs that already have a result are skipped.

00:12:23.754 --> 00:12:28.979
The list shows the result of every file. The copper
certificate was saved earlier, so it was skipped.

00:12:29.199 --> 00:12:37.751
For this product information sheet, the AI's answer was incomplete: the producer
is missing. Retry converts such files again, or you complete them by hand.

00:12:37.971 --> 00:12:44.077
Click a row to see the validation report of that document.
Review opens it in the form, next to its PDF.

00:12:44.297 --> 00:12:51.778
With Previous and Next, you move through the folder. Your edits are
saved to the folder automatically. Back to list returns to the results.

00:12:51.998 --> 00:12:59.497
If you drop a folder onto the generator instead, you can also
keep the results in the tab, and download them all as a ZIP file.

00:13:00.397 --> 00:13:07.610
Now the first way of working: entering a DRMD by hand.
Click New DRMD. The form and the PDF are cleared.

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:14.362
Fill in the tabs from Administrative to Statements. The
red stars and the status bar tell you what is still missing.

00:13:14.162 --> 00:13:18.019
Units, identifiers and all checks work in the same way, without AI.

00:13:18.239 --> 00:13:26.022
For a product information sheet, choose it as the title. Then no property
set can be certified, because only a certificate has certified values.

00:13:26.242 --> 00:13:30.873
To show your PDF next to the form, attach it on the Comment & documents tab.

00:13:31.773 --> 00:13:35.680
Let us use a new form to see how materials and their values are linked.

00:13:35.900 --> 00:13:44.527
On the Materials tab, click Add material. Enter the name, the RM code,
and the material identifier, for example the lot number, Lot-01.

00:13:44.747 --> 00:13:49.473
This document has a second material, with its own lot number, Lot-07.

00:13:50.373 --> 00:13:56.678
On the Properties tab, click Add property set. Under Linked
material, choose the material that these values belong to.

00:13:56.898 --> 00:14:06.122
Each table of the set can also be linked to one lot, under Linked batch / lot. The list
offers the lot and batch numbers of that material, as entered on the Materials tab.

00:14:06.342 --> 00:14:12.539
In the XML, the property set then points to the
identifier of its material, and the table points to its lot.

00:14:12.339 --> 00:14:17.204
So software can always tell which values belong to which material, and to which lot.

00:14:18.104 --> 00:14:19.927
There are three common cases.

00:14:20.147 --> 00:14:24.757
One material: its values are linked to it. This was the case of our copper certificate.

00:14:24.977 --> 00:14:31.850
Several materials in one document: give each material its
own identifier, and link each property set to its material.

00:14:32.070 --> 00:14:40.263
One material in several lots: if all lots have the same values, link the
property set to the material, and leave the tables at None (applies to all).

00:14:40.063 --> 00:14:44.877
If a lot has values of its own, give it its own table, and link that table to the lot.

00:14:45.877 --> 00:14:51.094
The third way: to edit an existing DRMD, click Import XML, and choose the file.

00:14:51.314 --> 00:14:55.521
The form is filled in again, and the embedded PDF opens on the left.

00:14:55.741 --> 00:15:04.999
A file saved by the generator opens exactly as it was saved, with the values still to
check and your verification marks. So you can stop your work and continue later.

00:15:05.899 --> 00:15:18.493
That is the DRMD AI Generator: enter a DRMD by hand, convert PDFs with AI one
by one or as a folder, or open and edit an XML file. Then check, validate, and save.

00:15:18.713 --> 00:15:24.101
For details about every element, see the DRMD
guidance document. Thank you for watching.
